                  "blocks": {
                    "text_jj3AKh": {
                      "type": "text",
                      "settings": {
                        "text": "<h4>Correct Toes may be eligible for HSA/FSA reimbursement when used to treat a qualifying medical condition.</h4>",
                        "width": "fit-content",
                        "max_width": "normal",
                        "alignment": "left",
                        "type_preset": "rte",
                        "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                        "font_size": "1rem",
                        "line_height": "normal",
                        "letter_spacing": "normal",
                        "case": "none",
                        "wrap": "pretty",
                        "color": "var(--color-foreground)",
                        "background": false,
                        "background_color": "#00000026",
                        "corner_radius": 0,
                        "padding-block-start": 0,
                        "padding-block-end": 16,
                        "padding-inline-start": 0,
                        "padding-inline-end": 0
                      },
                      "blocks": {}
                    },
                    "text_H9kdnH": {
                      "type": "text",
                      "settings": {
                        "text": "<p>Eligibility varies by provider, and a Letter of Medical Necessity may be required. <br/><br/>Please check with your plan administrator before purchasing.</p><ul><li>Keep the itemized receipt showing the product, purchase date, amount, and retailer.</li><li>If requested, obtain a Letter of Medical Necessity from a podiatrist, physician, physical therapist, or other qualified provider. The letter should identify:<br/><br/>- The diagnosed condition<br/>- Why Correct Toes is recommended<br/>- The expected duration of treatment</li></ul><p></p><ul><li>Submit the receipt and Letter of Medical Necessity through the HSA/FSA administrator’s reimbursement portal.</li><li>The plan administrator reviews the claim and issues reimbursement if approved.|</li></ul><p>Correct Toes does not provide the Letter of Medical Necessity. Please consult with your physician.</p>",
                        "width": "fit-content",
                        "max_width": "normal",
                        "alignment": "left",
                        "type_preset": "rte",
                        "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                        "font_size": "1rem",
