          },
          "blocks": {}
        },
        "text_Tae3iL": {
          "type": "text",
          "name": "t:names.text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Think of your foot’s arch like the Gateway Arch in Missouri—an engineering marvel held together by perfect balance and physics. Now imagine shifting one side of that arch just five feet to the left. What happens? It crumbles. Missouri’s skyline?</p><p><em><strong>Flat...</strong></em></p><p>Your foot works the same way. That elegant curve is supported by a key muscle and bone structure that stretches from the tip of your big toe, to your ankle. When narrow shoes squeeze your toes inward, it starts pushing that support away from its proper placement, which then weakens over time. And over years or decades, it can cause your arch to fall and other common foot conditions.</p>",
            "width": "fit-content",
            "max_width": "none",
            "alignment": "left",
            "type_preset": "rte",
            "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
            "font_size": "1rem",
            "line_height": "normal",
            "letter_spacing": "normal",
            "case": "none",
            "wrap": "pretty",
            "color": "var(--color-foreground)",
            "background": false,
            "background_color": "#00000026",
            "corner_radius": 0,
            "padding-block-start": 0,
            "padding-block-end": 0,
            "padding-inline-start": 0,
            "padding-inline-end": 0
          },
          "blocks": {}
        }
      },
